---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const seo = {
  page_description: "What makes a treat 'high value' in dog training?",
  canonical_url: null,
  featured_image: null,
  featured_image_alt: null,
  author_twitter_handle: null,
  open_graph_type: "article",
  no_index: false,
};
---

<Layout title="High Value Training Treats - DogSnacker Library" seo={seo}>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-16 px-4 prose max-w-none">
    <h1>The Hierarchy of Dog Treats</h1>
    <p class="lead text-xl">In dog training, not all treats are created equal. You need different 'currency' for different tasks.</p>
    <h2>Low Value Treats</h2>
    <p>Your dog's regular kibble. Great for practicing tricks they already know in the living room.</p>
    <h2>Medium Value Treats</h2>
    <p>Biscuits or crunchy store-bought treats. Good for walks around the neighborhood.</p>
    <h2>High Value Treats</h2>
    <p>Smelly, meaty, real food. Freeze-dried liver, salmon skin, or tripe. You need these when training recall at the park or working on reactivity, where the dog is highly distracted.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>
